{"id": "EUVD-2017-19026", "enisaUuid": "de2cc2be-5bd6-309c-a008-d13459cbe796", "description": "Broadstreet Ad Widget plugin for WordPress 2.2.0 before 2.12.0 contains a local file inclusion vulnerability that allows authenticated users to execute attacker-chosen PHP files by passing unsanitized input to require in views/modal/index.php. Attackers can supply directory traversal sequences in the 'step' parameter, optionally with a null byte, to include local files and execute PHP code. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-19.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:23", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://wpscan.com/vulnerability/caca21fe-56bf-4d4c-afc8-4a218e52f0a2", "https://packetstorm.news/files/id/144553/", "https://cxsecurity.com/issue/WLB-2017100084", "https://plugins.trac.wordpress.org/changeset/1628751/ad-widget", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/wordpress/ad-widget-lfi.yaml", "https://wordpress.org/plugins/ad-widget/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/broadstreet-ad-widget-wordpress-plugin-2.12.0-local-file-inclusion-via-step-parameter"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p32h-85vq-6f9p", "CVE-2017-20289"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ff23a88c-8fcf-340a-8e1d-471e158d33d8", "product": {"name": "Ad Widget", "vendor": {"name": "Broadstreet"}}, "product_version": "2.2.0 <2.12.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3d174fb9-8b45-3f70-a4f8-f343779bc787", "vendor": {"name": "Broadstreet"}}], "isExploited": false}